  "title": "1957 Cadillac Eldorado Seville: The Sleek Shark",
  "summary": "I love Cadillacs. Especially Eldorados. That, of course, has been well established. But believe it or not, I prefer the Eldorado Seville to the Eldorado Biarritz convertible. I’d rank both as gaudy and unquestionably luxurious, but there’s just something about those solid-roof Eldorados, produced from 1956-60, before the front-wheel-drive Eldorado personal luxury coupe replaced both […]",
